{"name":"Red Theatre","hex":"#6e3637","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"theatre","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of theater.","A cinema; movie theatre."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/theatre"}],"entries":[{"title":"Red House Theater","blocks":[{"text":"The Red House Theater, often called Hong Lo Red Play House, Red Theater, Ximen Honglou or Ximen Red House in English, is a historic theater in Ximending, Wanhua District, Taipei, Taiwan. The theater is located at 10 Chengdu Road."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Bangkah_Taipei_-_Red_House_Theater_-_facade_%282025%29_-_img_07.jpg/330px-Bangkah_Taipei_-_Red_House_Theater_-_facade_%282025%29_-_img_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_House_Theater","wikidata":"Q7304386"},{"title":"Theatre","blocks":[{"text":"Theatre or theater is a collaborative form of performing art that uses live performers, usually actors, to present experiences of a real or imagined event before a live audience in a specific place, often a stage. The performers may communicate this experience to the audience through combinations of gesture, speech, song, music, and dance."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Bernhardt_Hamlet2.jpg/330px-Bernhardt_Hamlet2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theatre","wikidata":"Q11635"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Sun_Wukong_at_Beijing_opera_-_Journey_to_the_West.jpg/500px-Sun_Wukong_at_Beijing_opera_-_Journey_to_the_West.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Sun_Wukong_at_Beijing_opera_-_Journey_to_the_West.jpg/500px-Sun_Wukong_at_Beijing_opera_-_Journey_to_the_West.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASun_Wukong_at_Beijing_opera_-_Journey_to_the_West.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Sculpture_Mode_Pose.jpg/500px-Sculpture_Mode_Pose.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Sculpture_Mode_Pose.jpg/1280px-Sculpture_Mode_Pose.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Sculpture_Mode_Pose.jpg/500px-Scu